                        ],
                        "form": "den Schöngeist"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "409a9a33-cdbb-4bc9-8a1c-d9de76684041",
                        "entry_id": "72f4e552-0de5-3574-8b0d-7505df7de790",
                        "tags": [
                            "accusative",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "die Schöngeister"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bcfdbf80-d35d-3e29-9bc4-03775d21a1f5",
                        "entry_id": "72f4e552-0de5-3574-8b0d-7505df7de790",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Person, die sich vornehmlich mit den \\\"schönen\\\" Künsten befasst"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "961eba2d-9cd1-4bd9-acc8-0a675384552d",
                                "sense_id": "bcfdbf80-d35d-3e29-9bc4-03775d21a1f5",
                                "text": "„Da mein Vater sah, daß die Madrider Schöngeister im Nu den größten Glasballon leerten, den er in der ganzen Stadt hatte finden können, ließ er aus Barcelona eine große Korbflasche kommen, von der Art, wie sie - gefüllt mit Wein - von den Matrosen des Mittelmeeres auf den Schiffen mitgeführt werden.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4dc722ae-374e-4cc0-8ee4-2f94dfa8298c",
                                "sense_id": "bcfdbf80-d35d-3e29-9bc4-03775d21a1f5",
                                "text": "„Cosenza ist eine Stadt, in der ein Mann von Welt gut leben kann, denn es gibt dort reiche Adlige, hübsche Frauen und Schöngeister.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9baa99d-c57c-40da-898e-da9b5d5b9446",
                                "sense_id": "bcfdbf80-d35d-3e29-9bc4-03775d21a1f5",
                                "text": "„Am meisten brachte alle denkenden Köpfe außer Fassung, daß dieser wundervolle Vertrag von einem jungen Diplomaten geplant und abgeschlossen worden war, der bis dahin nur für einen Schöngeist gegolten hatte.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4e6f526c-8748-46c4-9bdf-687232f7ef76",
                        "source_entry_id": "72f4e552-0de5-3574-8b0d-7505df7de790",
                        "source_sense_id": "bcfdbf80-d35d-3e29-9bc4-03775d21a1f5",
                        "target_lang_word": "aesthete",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "aesthete",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "caa1578b-dc38-3348-a422-26a70aef79b6",
                                        "entry_id": "de32d128-f284-3a63-aab5-c2ec9edae5f2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who cultivates an unusually high sensitivity to beauty, as in art or nature, often in a manner perceived to prioritize beauty over other qualities such as virtue and utility."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b06412aa-2bda-45d8-b6c1-fddc9b2601ea",
                                                "sense_id": "caa1578b-dc38-3348-a422-26a70aef79b6",
                                                "text": "I prefer to think of [literature] as providing a discipline of the sensibility—a special way of apprehending reality. But though I prefer such a conception, it gives rise to all sorts of misunderstandings […] To define literature in this fashion is to risk being called a mere aesthete and even an ecapist who refuses to face the harsh facts of life."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5485689-2e16-4817-9f24-2b404b82c94a",
                                                "sense_id": "caa1578b-dc38-3348-a422-26a70aef79b6",
                                                "text": "Because what the aesthete does is to say, “oh, I can transform any unpleasant experience into a moment of beauty.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47bed246-cb55-4d6f-abbd-33c8900d9aa7",
                                                "sense_id": "caa1578b-dc38-3348-a422-26a70aef79b6",
                                                "text": "Although Stanley was the political operator while Pick was the aesthete, it was Stanley who made the early running in Underground design."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d87a8cab-e7b2-4f8c-9250-6b2cbe2368d2",
                                                "sense_id": "caa1578b-dc38-3348-a422-26a70aef79b6",
                                                "text": "Since the days of Søren Kierkegaard, aesthetics – by him termed the aesthetic that is worshipped by the aesthete – has been accused of subjectivism and relativism. An aesthete is allegedly characterized by finding sensuous pleasure in particular phenomena, and by being different from the ethicist or the religious person in being unable to recognize or commit himself to anything universal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "74054682-1d36-40f2-a243-2e787f7738f6",
                        "source_entry_id": "72f4e552-0de5-3574-8b0d-7505df7de790",
                        "source_sense_id": "bcfdbf80-d35d-3e29-9bc4-03775d21a1f5",
                        "target_lang_word": "bel esprit",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bel esprit",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "467eedb3-aafc-3f89-8dbc-6f6906476a46",
                                        "entry_id": "e914a828-0e63-386d-bf92-e8191a8f261d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Genre d’esprit qui ne manque ni de distinction ni d’élégance, mais qui tombe facilement dans la prétention."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34aab9c7-b760-4419-9eda-d8d83168fdeb",
                                                "sense_id": "467eedb3-aafc-3f89-8dbc-6f6906476a46",
                                                "text": "La Garouffière, qui prétendait fort au bel esprit, se fit apporter un portefeuille."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "261b4f4d-90e9-4250-85f3-f11ad5954096",
                                                "sense_id": "467eedb3-aafc-3f89-8dbc-6f6906476a46",
                                                "text": "Cette chanson était le fait du receveur des postes, jeune citadin à lunettes et qui, au milieu de ces paysans, posait au bel esprit."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61cfa7ab-9cdb-3338-89df-2026b1f6de2b",
                                        "entry_id": "e914a828-0e63-386d-bf92-e8191a8f261d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne dont l’esprit est orné de connaissances agréables."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1088a954-3a6b-4d86-b172-895ff894faa9",
                                                "sense_id": "61cfa7ab-9cdb-3338-89df-2026b1f6de2b",
                                                "text": "Voiture est le premier qui fut en France ce qu’on appelle un bel esprit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59827306-d3be-4e43-9b63-02da9e276a94",
                                                "sense_id": "61cfa7ab-9cdb-3338-89df-2026b1f6de2b",
                                                "text": "Je le sais, Théobalde, vous êtes vieilli ; mais voudriez-vous que je crusse que vous êtes baissé, que vous n’êtes plus poëte ni bel esprit ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2b5e614-d97a-43b6-8474-109deee8fc7b",
                                                "sense_id": "61cfa7ab-9cdb-3338-89df-2026b1f6de2b",
                                                "text": "Ascagne est statuaire, Hégion fondeur, Eschine foulon, et Cydias bel esprit, c’est sa profession."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec1f18dc-8fd0-4640-9cca-cfa13700bcf8",
                                                "sense_id": "61cfa7ab-9cdb-3338-89df-2026b1f6de2b",
                                                "text": "Oui, allez dire qu’on peut nous voir ; c’est sans doute un bel esprit qui a ouï parler de nous."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c89d3df6-0e37-4e7d-933e-8e827e22f3ed",
                                                "sense_id": "61cfa7ab-9cdb-3338-89df-2026b1f6de2b",
                                                "text": "Vous recevez beaucoup de visites ? Quel bel esprit est des vôtres ?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "309c69ad-5339-4fb3-b0f0-51f143d40338",
                        "source_entry_id": "72f4e552-0de5-3574-8b0d-7505df7de790",
